Primo Levi guides the reader through the abysses of his life as a chemist and antifascist via the periodic table. 
The properties of each chemical element exemplify important figures and situations he met during his life. 
Full of wit and humble learnings, this book is an ideal substrate to his famous masterpiece "Se questo è un uomo?".
